  "sourceReview": [
    "Normal loadSave/decode/encode/saveGame/legacy migration code remains unchanged.",
    "Recovery is entered only with existing page state; complete committed state stays in memory even while an earlier presentation is cancelled.",
    "Both raw records are read exactly once for the recovery snapshot; a valid mirror remains usable behind absent, empty or corrupt primary records.",
    "Restore accepts only a still-missing null/null raw pair and reuses saveGame under the existing cross-tab Web Lock. Present empty, corrupt, legacy and current values all cause zero-write rejection.",
    "Read confirmation compares both original strings, not runId/revision/checksum or equal decoded payload.",
    "Import is guarded before and after file.text, at confirmation entry and again inside the write lock. Gameplay and new-run callbacks also guard the protected mode inside the lock.",
    "storage.key=null is handled, sessionStorage and unrelated keys are filtered, and later browser progress remains a candidate until explicit load."
  ],
  "openReviewNotes": [
    "Root browser validation is still required for real storage events, focus, downloads and animation cancellation.",
    "A repeated protected-page render originally focused the title only on first entry; this usability candidate was returned to the implementer for native verification.",
    "Web Locks coordinate cooperating app tabs. The read/compare sequence is not a universal atomic transaction against external writers that ignore this lock."
  ]
}
